  "worked_solution": "We're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(-2.18<Z<2.18).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14259374/assets/fb6af7fb416087d41fb826260cca7b504a599f2aa44a90e65f8fe2fc3ffaac43.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=Φ(z).\n$$\n\nSo, we express the required probability in terms of $Φ(z)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-2.18<Z<2.18) & =P(Z<2.18)-P(Z\\le -2.18) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 2.18)-P(Z\\le -2.18) \\\\  & =Φ(2.18)-Φ(-2.18)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we know that\n\n$$\nΦ(-2.18)=0.0146,\n$$\n\nbut we are not given $Φ(2.18).$ However, we can compute this using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(2.18) & =P(Z\\le 2.18) \\\\  & =P(Z\\ge -2.18) \\\\  & =1-P(Z<-2.18) \\\\  & =1-P(Z\\le -2.18) \\\\  & =1-Φ(-2.18) \\\\  & =1-0.0146 \\\\  & =0.9854\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-2.18<Z<2.18) & =Φ(2.18)-Φ(-2.18) \\\\  & =0.9854-0.0146 \\\\  & =0.9708.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
